v 3
d Draw interactive Google Charts (Visualization API) figures from Stata.
d Create a self-contained interactive HTML page, dashboard,
d or single embeddable iframe from any Stata dataset.
d
d Fourteen chart types: column, bar, line, area, combo, pie, donut,
d scatter, bubble, geo (country + US-state level), timeline, table
d (with built-in free-text search), histogram, divbar (Pew-style
d diverging stacked bar).  Filter dropdowns and range sliders
d (filters()) on every type.  Animation on most types.  Neutral
d default colors; tx2036style, an internal house style used in the
d authors' own workflows, is off by default.
d
d Self-contained -- no external Stata package dependencies.  The output
d HTML loads google.charts/loader.js from gstatic.com per Google ToS
d and therefore requires network access at view time.
d
d Requires: Stata 17+, network at view time for the resulting HTML.
d
d KW: google charts
d KW: visualization
d KW: interactive
d KW: html
d KW: dashboard
d KW: choropleth
d KW: divbar
d KW: likert
d
d Author: Eric A. Booth, Sr Researcher, Texas2036.org
d Support: eric.a.booth@gmail.com
d Distribution-Date: 20261112
d
f googlechart.ado
f googlechart.sthlp
f googlechart_writehtml.ado
f googlechart_engine.sthlp
f googlechart_appendfile.ado
f googlechart_embedjs.ado
